# =============================================================================
# frontend/.dockerignore
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Docker build-context exclusions for the CardDemo React 19 frontend image.
#
# Companion to frontend/Dockerfile (multi-stage build: a Node build stage that
# runs `npm ci` + `npm run build`, followed by an nginx stage that serves the
# compiled static assets). Everything NOT excluded here is transferred to the
# Docker daemon as the build context, so this file keeps that context both
# SMALL and CORRECT.
#
# Why this matters: the host's node_modules must NEVER be copied into the image.
# The builder stage installs a fresh, platform-correct dependency tree with
# `npm ci`; copying a host node_modules both bloats the context and can inject
# OS/arch-specific native binaries that break the container build.
#
# The following build inputs are intentionally NOT ignored and REMAIN copyable
# by the Dockerfile:
#   package.json, package-lock.json, vite.config.ts, tsconfig.json,
#   tsconfig.node.json, index.html, nginx.conf, src/, public/
#
# Patterns are kept consistent with the repository-root .gitignore (Respecting
# .gitignore rule, AAP 0.7.2); this file complements it, it does not replace it.
# =============================================================================

# --- Installed dependencies (reinstalled inside the image via `npm ci`) ------
node_modules

# --- Build output (produced inside the image, never copied from the host) ----
dist
build

# --- Test and build caches ---------------------------------------------------
coverage
.vite

# --- Version control ---------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore

# --- Docker files themselves (not needed inside the build context) -----------
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# --- Logs --------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# --- Local environment files (never bake local env into the image) -----------
# VITE_API_BASE_URL is supplied at build time as a Docker build ARG, not a file.
.env
.env.*

# --- OS / editor cruft -------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.vscode
.idea

# --- Documentation and tests (not required to build the image) ---------------
# Keeps the context lean; jest tests are not executed during the image build.
README*.md
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/*.spec.ts
**/*.spec.tsx
**/__tests__
